-- LIVENESS-EVERY-WORKER-1 (2026-10-12, metrics runtime_verified_share_24h 5.8 against >= 25 and threshold 10, agent_issues 2256
-- and 2157; pillar autonomy, PROBE-TRANSPORT-MONOCULTURE-1).
-- The runtime-liveness module of scripts/remediation_consumer.py (migration 2026-10-06-runtime-probe-transport.sql) runs a
-- runner-https probe from the GitHub runner every hour and files RUNTIME-PROBE-FAIL-1 after three straight failures, but only
-- eight hosts carry a contract (ai.qnfo.org, qnfo.org, fleet.qnfo.org, ideas.qnfo.org, personal.qnfo.org, ipatent.qnfo.org,
-- papers.qnfo.org, q08.org). The other 21 live workers are observed only from inside the account (fleet-control service probes,
-- the issue-1190 artifact) and by D1 reads, so a day's verifications are 6109 d1-query rows against 405 runner-https rows.
-- Every live worker in service_registry now has a standing liveness contract on its /health (status 200 and a version field, the
-- same shape every fleet /health answers; measured 2026-10-12T16:27Z: all 21 answer 200 with "version"). 21 more runtime
-- observations an hour is about 500 a day, so the share moves from 5.8 toward 12 by the next day's window, and a worker that
-- stops answering from outside the account files its own issue. A worker that is retired takes its row out in its retirement
-- migration (the Rollback line above removes them all).
